# FCE Use of English — reuse shells first

When adding or fixing **Use of English** tasks under `use-of-english/` (FCE / Mastering B2):

## Mandatory order

1. **Search** `use-of-english/` + `css/part*.css` + `js/*-core.js` for the closest **Part** or workbook pattern.
2. **Reuse** that page shell, gap classes, buttons, feedback — **new data/JSON only**.
3. **Do not** build a new layout on `mastering-b2-page-skin.css` alone for UoE gap tasks unless no shell fits — say why briefly.

## Shell map (FCE UoE)

| Task type | Shell CSS | Engine / etalon |
|-----------|-----------|-----------------|
| Part 1 MC cloze | `css/part1-mc-cloze.css` + `body.part1-mc-fce-theme` | `js/part1-mc-cloze-core.js` — `use-of-english/part1-mc-cloze/index.html` |
| Part 2 open cloze | `css/part2-open-cloze.css` + `body.part2-open-body` | `js/part2-open-cloze-core.js` — `use-of-english/part2-open-cloze/index.html` |
| Part 3 word formation (exam text + ROOT) | `css/cpe-uoe-part3-wf-shell.css` | `use-of-english/part3-word-formation/unit2-art-of-sushi.html` |
| Part 4 key word transformation | inline tokens = Part 2 panel (`#1d2b4a`) | `use-of-english/part4-key-word-transformation/unit1.html` |
| Workbook gap-fill / sentence completion | **`part2-open-cloze.css`** (`.part2-open-page`, `.part2-open-task`, `.gap`, `.part2-btn-*`, `.part2-feedback`) | `use-of-english/unit2/affixes/` |
| Workbook blog error hunt | `part2-open-cloze.css` + `css/fce-vocab-blog-gap.css` | `use-of-english/unit2/affixes-blog/` |
| Hearts / drill trainers | existing hearts page in `use-of-english/unitN/` | e.g. `unit8/word-formation-adjectives-hearts/` |

## Hard UX (all UoE gap tasks)

- Gaps: class **`.gap`** inside **`.part2-open-task`** (or Part 3 `.gap-wrap` for exam WF).
- Check feedback: **`.part2-feedback.show`** — not a custom `.wf-feedback`.
- Buttons: **`.part2-btn-check`** / **`.part2-btn-reset`** — not ad-hoc `.btn-check`.
- **No spoilers before Check** — hints/keys hidden until wrong answer on check (`.p2-inline-key`, `[hidden]`).
- Back link on FCE unit pages: **`css/mastering-b2-back-link.css`** pill (`.back`).

## Workbook add-ons

Small layout unique to one workbook (e.g. prefix groups in affixes Ex. 1) may live in a **thin scoped CSS** file (e.g. `fce-word-formation-affixes.css`) that **imports nothing new** — only extends the Part 2 tokens (`--p2-*`). **Never** duplicate full page chrome.

## CPE vs FCE

- **Shared shells** (`part2-open-cloze.css`, `cpe-uoe-part3-wf-shell.css`) are OK for mechanics — route/content stays in `use-of-english/` per track.
- Do **not** link FCE unit hubs to CPE-only UoE folders without track separation (`fce-cpe-content-folder-split.mdc`).

## If unsure

- Sentence gaps / open answers → copy **`part2-open-cloze`** markup.
- Exam passage + CAPS root word → copy **`part3-word-formation`**.
- MC cloze → **`part1-mc-cloze-core.js`**.
